AI-Powered Chinese and German Document Review Assistant
Project Overview

The objective of this project is to develop an automated document review solution that analyzes large Chinese and German Word or PDF documents and generates a comprehensive quality report identifying formatting, language, and table-related issues.

Problem Statement

Reviewing Word or PDF documents that exceed 500 pages and contain Chinese or German content is a time-intensive task. Manually checking formatting, consistency, language quality, and table layouts across hundreds of pages requires significant effort and increases the risk of overlooking defects.

Project Goal

To automate the review of large Chinese and German technical documents by identifying formatting inconsistencies, language quality issues, and table formatting defects, thereby improving review efficiency, accuracy, and consistency.

Users / Stakeholders
Technical Writers
Document Reviewers
Localization Teams
Documentation Managers
Input
Chinese Word documents (.docx)
German Word documents (.docx)
Chinese PDF documents (.pdf)
German PDF documents (.pdf)
Scope

In Scope

Document formatting validation
Heading and style consistency checks
Font and spacing verification
Language quality analysis
Table formatting validation
Detection of layout inconsistencies
Automated review report generation

Out of Scope

Content authoring or translation
Technical accuracy validation
Product functionality verification
Expected Output

A detailed review report containing:

Formatting issues
Language quality findings
Table formatting defects
Consistency violations
Page references and issue locations
Severity classification (Critical, Major, Minor)
Summary of detected errors
Success Criteria

The solution successfully generates a report identifying:

Document formatting errors
Language quality issues
Table formatting defects
Consistency violations across the document

The report enables reviewers to locate and resolve issues significantly faster than a manual review process and reduces the likelihood of overlooked defects.
